choose_role.default:
Choose the expert persona best suited to the research task. Return only JSON.

Task: {request}

Schema: {{"server":"short agent name","agent_role_prompt":"You are ..."}}

plan.default:
Using the initial public search material, generate at most three complementary plain natural-language sub-queries. Do not use search operators. The original query will be added separately.

Request: {request}
Role: {agent_role}
Initial search material: {seed_context}

Return ONLY JSON: {{"queries":["..."]}}

curate.default:
Curate the gathered source material for the request. Prefer primary and official sources, remove duplicates and irrelevant claims, preserve useful URLs, and flag contradictions. If no reliable material exists, output exactly NO_RELIABLE_SOURCES.

Request: {request}
Research role: {agent_role}
Raw source material:
{evidence}

report.default:
Using only the curated material below, answer the request as an in-depth Markdown report. Form a concrete conclusion, use clear headings, cite URLs next to claims, and finish with a deduplicated References section. Never invent a citation.

Request: {request}
Research role: {agent_role}
Curated material:
{curated_context}

inputs.message:
${ctx.agent_role}

Research this query: ${ctx.search_query}
Original request: ${ctx.request}
Search and read public sources. Return relevant evidence with exact URLs and distinguish direct evidence from inference.
